<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44007" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sessĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		sedeo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>be longing to
			sitting</i>, <i>fit for sitting upon</i> (only in the
			poets and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergum (equi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 401</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obba,</span>”
				i. e. <i>with a broad foot</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 148</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pira minimo pe diculo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 15, 16, § 56</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of plants, <i>low</i>, <i>dwarf</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus lactucae,</span>”
				<i>growing low</i>, <i>spreading</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 8, 38, § 125</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 47, 8</span></i> (for which: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sedens lactuca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 48, 9</span></i>
			): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folium (brassicae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 8, 41, § 140</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Oct. 11, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
